        "q": "Will artificial turf raise my stormwater bill?",
        "a": "It can, where a jurisdiction classes it impervious. Myrtle Beach bills on an equivalent residential unit of 5,000 square feet of impervious area; North Myrtle Beach uses 3,500. A 2,000 square foot back-yard install is roughly 0.4 of a Myrtle Beach unit and 0.57 of a North Myrtle Beach one — small for a homeowner, real on a commercial parcel, where Horry County scales the charge by impervious percentage."
